{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150@rel:R23-11#08eae6af","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R23-11","content":"[SWS_SecOC_00150]⌈\nWhen SecOC_TriggerTransmit is called by the PduR module and the SecOC\nmodule is not able to provide a Secured I-PDU to the lower layer (no Secured I-PDU\navailable), the SecOC module shall return the call with E_NOT_OK.\n⌋(SRS_SecOC_00010, SRS_SecOC_00012, SRS_SecOC_00013)\nFinally, when the lower layer confirms the processing of the Secured I-PDU via\nPduR_<Lo>TxConfirmation (the result can be positive, if the PDU was\nsuccessfully sent or negative if a transmission was not possible), the confirmation is\nforwarded to the SecOC module by calling SecOC_TxConfirmation. In turn, the\nSecOC module passes the result of the transmission process of the Authentic I-PDU\nat the PduR module so that the PduR module could forward the result via\n<Up>_TxConfirmation to the upper layer module which was the source of the\noriginal I-PDU (see SWS_SecOC_00063).\nDuring triggered transmission, the update rates of the upper layer modules and the\nlower layer modules might be different. Thus, the lower layer module might request a\nnew transmission of a Secured I-PDU while the upper layer has not updated the\nAuthentic I-PDU. In this case, the SecOC module supports the repeated transmission\nof the Authentic I-PDU by means of an updated Secure I-PDU. Thus, it has to\npreserve the Authentic I-PDU until the Secured I-PDU has been sent and its\ntransmission has been confirmed by a means of SecOC_TxConfirmation. In this\ncase, the SecOC module treats the existing Authentic I-PDU as new and re-\nauthenticates it during the subsequent call to the SecOC_MainFunctionTx.","meta":{"source_pdf":"SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication.pdf","source_page":44,"trigger_kind":"snippet_ingest"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+00:00","text_key":"5d18e01ffa93"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","release":"R25-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00150","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11","text_releases":["R23-11"],"presence_only":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"unchecked":["R18-10"]},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"SecOC","cluster":"security","page":"","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R19-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"CP"},"evidence":{"figures":[],"snippets":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_SECOC_SECTION_6_Requirements_traceability","doc":"SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication","p":18,"rel":[],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"deterministic","why":"Cited verbatim in the snippet (deterministic citation).","n":131,"x":"6 Requirements traceability The following table references the requirem